Laya decision models, ONNX exports for Nekko Agent

These files are ONNX conversions of the Laya checkpoints by Convai Innovations,
published under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE, copied from
https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya):

  laya-en                convaiinnovations/laya @ 55cf4c4ebb4ebe31b2550e8bdf3bd21b99753851
  laya-multilingual      convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual @ e4e9ddf21a7b1903b7acffd8814ad4307bf63a67
  laya-typed-decisions   convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions @ 1a793eb568e6718f15941d08f85432581df534e3

  https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations

Changes made by Nekko Labs (scripts/decision-models/ in
https://github.com/nekko-labs/nekko-agent):

- model.onnx: the checkpoint's weights exported to ONNX with laya's own exporter
  recipe (torch dynamo, opset 18, dynamic shapes); `allowzero` cleared on every
  Reshape node, which does not change the computation.
- model_fp16.onnx: model.onnx converted to float16 weights and activations, with
  the rotary-embedding angle computation kept in float32.
- model_int8.onnx: model.onnx with weight-only 8-bit block quantization of its
  MatMul weights.
- tokenizer.json, tokenizer_config.json, rl_agent_config.json and config.json
  are copied unchanged from the checkpoint (config.json is its encoder/config.json).

The weights are otherwise unchanged. The converted models answer the 60-request
golden set of Nekko Agent's decision runtime the same way the official `laya`
package (0.3.22) does; see docs/decision-models.md in the Nekko Agent repository.
